Build the classifier's label tensor on the device the rest of the model uses.

pytorch_DGCNN/main.py moves features and labels to the GPU only when
`cmd_args.mode == 'gpu'` (lines 107-111), and the classifier likewise (line
214) -- except at line 129, where the labels subsampled for the MLP are
created with an unconditional `.cuda()`. So STRGNN cannot run on a CPU at all:
with `_GPU=-1` (`graflag run --no-gpu`) on a node whose GPU is hidden from
the container, the first batch raised

    labels = torch.LongTensor(labels).cuda()
    RuntimeError: Found no NVIDIA driver on your system.

and with the GPU visible it raised `Expected all tensors to be on the same
device ... cpu and cuda:0` in nll_loss instead. The guard below is the one
upstream uses six lines earlier; on a GPU it does exactly what line 129 did.
It is the only unguarded CUDA call in upstream's Python.

Generated with `git diff` against the tree SOURCE_REF pins.

diff --git a/pytorch_DGCNN/main.py b/pytorch_DGCNN/main.py
index 9162637..31eb874 100644
--- a/pytorch_DGCNN/main.py
+++ b/pytorch_DGCNN/main.py
@@ -126,7 +126,9 @@ class Classifier(nn.Module):
             node_feat, edge_feat, labels = feature_label
         embed = self.gnn(batch, node_feat, edge_feat)
         labels = [labels[i] for i in range(0,labels.shape[0],5)]
-        labels = torch.LongTensor(labels).cuda()
+        labels = torch.LongTensor(labels)
+        if cmd_args.mode == "gpu":
+            labels = labels.cuda()
         return self.mlp(embed, labels)
 
     def output_features(self, batch_graph):
